<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680.jpg"><img decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="1260" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-124238" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-scaled.jpg 1707w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-200x300.jpg 200w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/DSC08680-1365x2048.jpg 1365w" sizes="(max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>The other week I made a <a shot href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2026/08/27/the-weather-in-coconino-county/">calendrical display</a> for the eink thing I have.  The problem is that I don&#8217;t really use a calendar &#8212; I guess the main reason is because I hate planning, but the other reason is because I really dislike all the calendar entry interfaces I&#8217;ve used.</p>
<p>I haven&#8217;t used all that many, though, so I may well be missing some ingenious calendar out there.  But what I&#8217;ve been resentfully using is the standard Google calendar on Android.</p>
<p>I filmed one of my interactions with this thing, and I swear &#8212; I didn&#8217;t try to make it more awkward than it is for me:</p>
<p><video controls loop muted poster="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/posteruuuhIM001.jpg"><source src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/video-52kEGH.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></p>
<p>I&#8217;d be climbing up the walls if I were to try to use it more than I do now &#8212; I just put the absolute bare necessities in there, like dentist appointments and Boris shows.  (One coming up in November!)</p>
<p>But now I have this calendar in the hall&#8230;  wouldn&#8217;t it be nice to have it display more stuff?  Stuff that I really should be remembering, anyway?</p>
<p>There&#8217;s also <tt>org-gcal</tt>, if you&#8217;re in the Org ecosystem&#8230;  but&#8230;  I&#8217;m not.</p>
<p>Does a command line interface to Google Calendar work?  Because I want to have the calendar in my pocket, too.  And&#8230;  <a href="https://github.com/insanum/gcalcli" data-cached-time="2026-09-08T16:32:43" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/cache-2026-09-08-web.webp">Yes, there&#8217;s gcalcli.</a>  (Which I noticed hasn&#8217;t been updated for two years and is probably going to be deprecated, but it works for now, so I haven&#8217;t bothered to redo my code.)</p>
<p>After going through the byzantine process on Google Cloud Console to create an &#8220;application&#8221;:</p>
<p><a class="cimage" href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-08.jpeg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async"  src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-08.jpeg" alt="" width="840" height="712" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-124239" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-08.jpeg 1528w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-08-300x254.jpeg 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-08-1024x869.jpeg 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-08-768x651.jpeg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Yes!  You have to create a logo!  Behold my magnificent logo!</p>
<p>Anyway, after all that&#8230;  tada:</p>
<p><video controls loop muted poster="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/posterZckwSN001-scaled.jpg"><source src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/video-Zli3d8.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></p>
<p>Yes!  The system works!</p>
<p>It does the normal Do What I Mean Thing &#8212; &#8220;fri 9&#8221; means &#8220;next Friday at 9am&#8221;, and &#8220;aug 11 1930&#8221; means &#8220;half past seven on August 11&#8221;, etc:</p>
<p><video controls loop muted poster="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/poster1pM3xN001-scaled.jpg"><source src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/video-GYcwAp.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></p>
<p>I&#8217;m freee!  I never have to enter a calendar entry on the mobile phone ever again!</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve put the resulting code on <a href="https://github.com/larsmagne/gcal.el" data-cached-time="2026-09-08T16:40:46" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/cache-2026-09-08-web-1.webp">Microsoft Github</a>.</p>
